1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,868
Could a yeti really survive in

2
00:00:01,868 --> 00:00:02,566
the Himalayas?

3
00:00:02,566 --> 00:00:04,754
Let's build one.

4
00:00:05,377 --> 00:00:06,792
In Sherpa and Tibetan stories,

5
00:00:06,792 --> 00:00:07,792
it's a huge,

6
00:00:07,868 --> 00:00:09,282
hairy walker of the high snow.

7
00:00:10,057 --> 00:00:11,415
But a big body sinks in

8
00:00:11,415 --> 00:00:12,150
deep snow.

9
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:13,906
So you grow wide,

10
00:00:13,906 --> 00:00:14,453
furry feet,

11
00:00:14,453 --> 00:00:15,716
like a snowshoe hare.

12
00:00:16,094 --> 00:00:17,170
They spread your weight,

13
00:00:17,170 --> 00:00:18,414
so you stay on top.

14
00:00:19,094 --> 00:00:20,208
But the air up here is

15
00:00:20,208 --> 00:00:20,678
thin.

16
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:22,566
So you tune your body for

17
00:00:22,566 --> 00:00:23,433
low oxygen,

18
00:00:23,642 --> 00:00:24,471
like the yak,

19
00:00:24,623 --> 00:00:26,019
whose genes are built for high

20
00:00:26,019 --> 00:00:26,716
altitude.

21
00:00:27,434 --> 00:00:28,736
But then winter comes,

22
00:00:28,736 --> 00:00:30,037
and there's nothing to eat.

23
00:00:30,604 --> 00:00:31,811
So you sleep through it,

24
00:00:31,811 --> 00:00:32,774
like a brown bear,

25
00:00:32,774 --> 00:00:34,641
living on stored fat for months.

26
00:00:35,491 --> 00:00:36,810
Now look at what you built.

27
00:00:37,585 --> 00:00:38,170
A big,

28
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:39,093
furry bear.

29
00:00:39,717 --> 00:00:41,151
In twenty seventeen,

30
00:00:41,151 --> 00:00:43,244
scientists tested nine yeti samples.

31
00:00:44,113 --> 00:00:45,207
One was a dog.

32
00:00:45,887 --> 00:00:47,471
The other eight were Asian bears.

33
00:00:48,321 --> 00:00:49,736
And the name yeti comes from

34
00:00:49,736 --> 00:00:51,622
Tibetan words meaning rock bear.

35
00:00:52,113 --> 00:00:54,093
So the legend isn't empty.

36
00:00:54,849 --> 00:00:56,376
It grew from a real animal.

